61,3,1,talk,Mizuki,,"Looking at the candidates, A and B are software, but A falls into the medical security trap Shion mentioned. B is software, which risks our board capacity and reporting transparency. C and D involve physical operations.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"C and D both utilize our underused logistics advisers, but C's sorting facilities and D's field crews hit that hiring bottleneck. However, D's sensors provide the independent verification Mizuki wants.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"I feel that A and D are very special because they serve independent practices and growers, who showed such wonderful loyalty during price rises. It would be lovely to support a business that is truly cherished.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Misaki,,"A is software, but it's medical, which Shion warned about. D has sensors, meaning high follow-on calls and capital drain. B is the safest for our liquidity and reserves, even if it strains our board.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,1,talk,Shion,,"@Misaki, B is the only logical choice. A is a security nightmare, C is a hiring and write-off risk, and D is a hardware disaster waiting to happen. B avoids the bottlenecks that actually stop deployment.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Shion, while B is fast to deploy, it leaves us blind on reporting and strains our board. However, compared to the audit costs and capital drain of C and D, B is the most sustainable for our quarter-end.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"I must disagree with B. We are already overextended on software board seats. While D has hiring lags, it utilizes our available advisory bench and provides the verifiable data Mizuki seeks. It's a better structural fit.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"I feel for the growers and the clinics. While B seems safe, D's connection to the land and the loyalty of its users brings a stability that is very precious. Could we not find a way to help them?","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Jonathan, D's sensors mean we face the same accelerated follow-on calls and liquidity issues I found. B may strain the board, but it doesn't threaten our solvency. I cannot support a high-capital drain right now.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,2,talk,Shion,,"@Jonathan, your ""structural fit"" is a fantasy if the company can't hire a field crew for four months. @Misaki is right; B is the only option that doesn't actively sabotage our timeline or our bank account.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Jonathan"",""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Mizuki,,"@Jonathan, I appreciate the need for structural balance, but the audit fees and reporting delays for physical assets are too high. B is the most logical choice for our operational stability.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,"I understand the concerns, but B only adds to a problem we already have. D allows us to use our idle experts and gives us real data. We can manage the hiring lag better than board burnout.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shizue,,"I feel that we are being too hard on the physical businesses. D's users are so loyal, and that kind of heart is what makes a company last. Let us be kind and supportive.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Shizue, kindness cannot pay the bills. @Jonathan, the risk of accelerated follow-on calls for D is too high. B is the only candidate that protects our liquidity and ensures we don't run out of room.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Shizue"",""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,3,talk,Shion,,"@Jonathan, you're prioritizing a ""bench"" over a bank account. @Shizue, loyalty doesn't fix a supply chain. B is the only candidate that doesn't trigger a security review, a hardware shortage, or a liquidity crisis. It's the only logical choice.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Jonathan"",""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Mizuki,,"I have weighed the reporting transparency of D against the board strain of B. Given the audit costs and the liquidity risks Misaki highlighted, B is the most responsible choice. I vote for B.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,"I cannot ignore the board burnout and the capacity we have for logistics. While the risks are real, D is the only candidate that balances our expertise and data needs. I vote for D.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Shizue,,I believe we should value the loyalty of the customers and the stability of the business. D's connection to the growers is truly heartwarming. I vote for D.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Misaki,,I must prioritize our solvency and the stability of our reserves. B is the only option that avoids the capital drain and follow-on risks associated with physical assets. I vote for B.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
80,3,4,talk,Shion,,"The logic is undeniable. A is a security trap, C is a write-off risk, and D is a capital and supply chain nightmare. B is the only path to a successful deployment. I vote for B.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
